****************************************************************
Geode extension grammar for ISO/IEC 39075 GQL.

Supplementary productions layered over the vendored ISO artifact
(grammar/ISO_IEC_39075.bnf.txt), parsed and merged by
tests/grammar_test.zig ("geode extension grammar parses and merges
cleanly over ISO grammar"). Productions here may reference ISO
nonterminals and may redefine ISO productions to add alternatives —
per ebnf's Grammar.mergeFrom, a redefinition REPLACES the ISO
production entirely, so every redefinition below restates the
original ISO alternatives verbatim and appends the Geode addition.

NOTE ON NOTATION: only text ABOVE the first `<name> ::=` header is
ignored by ebnf's bnf.parse — text between two productions is parsed
as trailing content of the PRECEDING production, so this file carries
no free-standing prose between rules. Rationale and source citations
live in `!!` lines inside each production body instead, and the full
narrative survey lives in .superpowers/sdd/task-B3-report.md.

Extensions covered (verified against src/{token,ast,parser,
language_metadata}.zig on branch feat/grammar-verification):
  1. Top-level SCAN and CREATE CONSTRAINT statement forms (ASSERT/SCAN
     keywords, .geode_extension in language_metadata.zig).
  2. `@` field annotations + PRIMARY KEY in CREATE GRAPH TYPE field
     definitions (Field-Level Encryption extension).
  3. VECTOR / UUID / JSON predefined types (.geode_extension types).
  4. `^` circumflex power operator (token.zig `caret`).
  5. Geode scalar/vector/graph functions (.geode_extension functions) —
     call-syntax-only notes; no new production needed.
  6. Parser-flag-gated extension functions found while auditing
     src/parser.zig:26-48 (ts_extensions) that have no
     language_metadata.zig entry at all — flagged as a documentation
     gap rather than silently dropped.
****************************************************************

<geode GQL-program> ::=
    <GQL-program>

<statement> ::=
    !! Redefines ISO_IEC_39075.bnf.txt:143-146 <statement>, restating its
    !! 3 original alternatives and appending the 2 Geode statement forms.
    <linear catalog-modifying statement>
  | <linear data-modifying statement>
  | <composite query statement>
  | <geode scan statement>
  | <geode create constraint statement>

<geode scan statement> ::=
    !! src/parser.zig:759-768 (`.SCAN => blk_scan: ...`). SCAN keyword is
    !! .geode_extension in src/language_metadata.zig:220.
    SCAN [ { VALUE | VALUES } ]

<geode create constraint statement> ::=
    !! src/parser.zig:5104-5196 (`parseCreateConstraint`). CREATE
    !! CONSTRAINT is entirely absent from the ISO artifact (only the bare
    !! pre-reserved word CONSTRAINT appears, ISO_IEC_39075.bnf.txt:2982).
    !! ASSERT is .geode_extension in src/language_metadata.zig:99.
    CREATE CONSTRAINT [ IF NOT EXISTS ] <identifier>
        { <geode constraint iso clause>
        | <geode constraint legacy clause> }

<geode constraint iso clause> ::=
    !! src/parser.zig:5133-5162, 5199-5281 (`parseConstraintCondition`,
    !! the ISO-flavored `FOR (n:Label) REQUIRE ...` form).
    FOR <left paren> <identifier> <colon> <identifier> <right paren>
        REQUIRE <geode constraint requirement>

<geode constraint requirement> ::=
    <left paren> <geode property name list> <right paren> IS NODE KEY
  | <geode property reference> IS NOT NULL
  | <geode property reference> IS UNIQUE

<geode constraint legacy clause> ::=
    !! src/parser.zig:5164-5186, 5283-5355 (legacy `ON :Label ASSERT ...`
    !! form, `parseConstraintConditionLegacy`).
    ON [ <colon> ] <identifier> ASSERT <geode constraint legacy requirement>

<geode constraint legacy requirement> ::=
    EXISTS <left paren> <identifier> <right paren>
  | <left paren> <geode property name list> <right paren> IS { NODE KEY | UNIQUE }
  | <identifier> IS UNIQUE

<geode property reference> ::=
    <identifier> [ <period> <identifier> ]

<geode property name list> ::=
    <identifier> [ { <comma> <identifier> }... ]

<property type> ::=
    !! Field-Level Encryption extension. Redefines
    !! ISO_IEC_39075.bnf.txt:1313-1314 <property type> to append the
    !! optional Geode field modifiers; restates the sole original
    !! alternative unchanged. src/ast.zig:602-636
    !! (FieldAnnotation/FieldDefinition/CreateGraphTypeStatement, "Geode
    !! Extension"); src/parser.zig:5885-5985 (`parseFieldDefinitions`).
    <property name> [ <typed> ] <property value type> [ <geode field modifiers> ]

<geode field definition> ::=
    <property type>

<geode field modifiers> ::=
    [ PRIMARY KEY ] [ <geode field annotation>... ]

<geode field annotation> ::=
    <commercial at> <geode annotation name>
        [ <left paren> [ <geode annotation argument list> ] <right paren> ]

<geode annotation name> ::=
    ENCRYPTED
  | SEARCHABLE

<geode annotation argument list> ::=
    <geode annotation argument> [ { <comma> <geode annotation argument> }... ]

<geode annotation argument> ::=
    !! src/parser.zig:5931-5950 skips a balanced paren run verbatim
    !! without structurally validating its contents; modeled here as an
    !! optional `name:` label over a general value expression (covers
    !! the observed `algorithm: 'AES256-GCM'`-style keyword arguments as
    !! well as bare literals/identifiers).
    [ <identifier> <colon> ] <value expression>

<predefined type> ::=
    !! Redefines ISO_IEC_39075.bnf.txt:1331-1338 <predefined type> to
    !! append <geode predefined type>; restates the 7 original
    !! alternatives unchanged. VECTOR/UUID/JSON are .geode_extension in
    !! src/language_metadata.zig:1207-1210.
    <boolean type>
  | <character string type>
  | <byte string type>
  | <numeric type>
  | <temporal type>
  | <reference value type>
  | <immaterial value type>
  | <geode predefined type>

<geode predefined type> ::=
    VECTOR
  | UUID
  | JSON

<factor> ::=
    !! ISO already has POWER(base, exponent) call syntax (<power
    !! function>, ISO_IEC_39075.bnf.txt:2103-2105) but no infix operator.
    !! Redefines ISO_IEC_39075.bnf.txt:2004-2005 <factor> to append an
    !! optional, left-associative power suffix; restates the sole
    !! original alternative unchanged. src/token.zig:39 (`caret`);
    !! src/parser.zig:3330-3341 (`parsePowerExpr`, left-associative
    !! while-loop left-fold (a^b)^c, binds tighter than * and /).
    [ <sign> ] <numeric primary> [ <geode circumflex> <factor> ]

<geode circumflex> ::=
    ^

<geode call syntax scalar functions> ::=
    !! None of the functions noted in this and the next two productions
    !! introduce new call *syntax* — every one is invoked as an ordinary
    !! `name ( args )` expression, the same shape already used for ISO
    !! builtins (COUNT(...), ABS(...), POWER(...,...), etc.) and
    !! validated semantically (not syntactically) by
    !! src/parser.zig:4224 (`validateBuiltinCall`). Validation dispatch:
    !! vectorf32, vectori32 are in the builtin_map (src/parser.zig:4161-4222);
    !! icontains and all other Geode functions are accepted via the generic
    !! unknown-function pass-through (src/parser.zig:4231 `orelse return true`).
    !! No new production is needed for reachability; these notes exist purely
    !! to account for every `.geode_extension` function entry in
    !! src/language_metadata.zig. icontains(str, search) — case-insensitive
    !! CONTAINS. src/language_metadata.zig:741-752.

<geode call syntax vector functions> ::=
    !! vectorf32(list), vectori32(list), vector_l2(v1, v2),
    !! vector_cosine(v1, v2), vector_dot(v1, v2), distance(v1, v2),
    !! similarity(v1, v2), cosine(v1, v2), euclidean(v1, v2),
    !! manhattan(v1, v2). src/language_metadata.zig:969-1083.

<geode call syntax graph functions> ::=
    !! indegree(node), outdegree(node) — graph degree functions.
    !! src/language_metadata.zig:1159-1177.

<geode ts extension functions note> ::=
    !! Found while auditing src/parser.zig:26-48 for extension-gating
    !! parser flags per the task brief. last_value, value_at, sample_by,
    !! interpolate, moving_avg, rate, derivative, time_bucket —
    !! time-series builtins gated by Parser.ts_extensions
    !! (src/parser.zig:38, enforced at src/parser.zig:4181-4189).
    !! Undocumented in language_metadata.zig (documentation gap,
    !! flagged rather than silently dropped). Call-syntax-only; no new
    !! production needed.

<geode undocumented builtins note> ::=
    !! lat_lon(...), lat_lon_alt(...), geo_point(...), jsonb(...),
    !! geometry_from_text(...) — present in src/parser.zig's Builtin
    !! enum (src/parser.zig:4161-4190) but absent from
    !! language_metadata.zig. Call-syntax-only; no new production
    !! needed.
